Writing with your fingers is the least effective way of using E--it
smudges almost immediately.

Use the /fire to burn E instead of trying to write it in the dust with
your fingers.

Once burned into the ground, it's permanent (barring
polymorphing/teleporting it, cancellation, etc) and you can stand on it
and throw rocks at the ants, melee them, or whatever with impunity.
(If you write it in the dust, trying to melee is likely to wipe out the
E and leave you open to attack)

/lightning does the same but blinds you in the process.

/digging or an athame (e.g. Magicbane) does a semi-permanent E; it's a
lot less likely to rub out than writing in the dust, but still
possible.

Alternatively, run for a corridor or other choke-point (preferably with
a pet nearby to buffer between you and them), keep close to the stairs
or have a /teleport, /digging, or other escape plan, use missile
weapons to take them down at range, fill squares with E with an item on
them to block the ants, etc.



